{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CeatmQt4u8DomLRDbknBrN","type":"tool_result","content":"819\tThis is the absent-component pattern (thread 3) in Domain 2 clothing. The NetworkPolicy object is valid and accepted by the API server; nothing enforces it unless the installed CNI plugin implements policy. Creating the object is half the transaction.\n820\t\n821\t**A is wrong** — this is same-namespace traffic and the frontend Pods are not selected by any policy, so their egress is unrestricted. The both-ends rule applies only when *both* ends are selected by policies. **C is wrong** and is the most instructive distractor: NetworkPolicy is additive and allow-only, with no deny rule at all. If you picked C, thread 9 is soft; go back to Ch 10 §6 and Ch 12 §3. **D is wrong** — `podSelector` alone covers same-namespace sources; `namespaceSelector` is for crossing namespaces.\n822\t\n823\t*Chapters: 10 (NetworkPolicy semantics, absent-component pattern), 9 (CNI as the pluggable interface).*"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42d6f0ae-7b0a-48db-a252-693e8a9bb7f6","uuid":"9b842f43-070b-4335-b4cc-bddc6b6c063f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:58:42.794Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-19\\draft-v1.md","content":"This is the absent-component pattern (thread 3) in Domain 2 clothing. The NetworkPolicy object is valid and accepted by the API server; nothing enforces it unless the installed CNI plugin implements policy. Creating the object is half the transaction.\n\n**A is wrong** — this is same-namespace traffic and the frontend Pods are not selected by any policy, so their egress is unrestricted. The both-ends rule applies only when *both* ends are selected by policies. **C is wrong** and is the most instructive distractor: NetworkPolicy is additive and allow-only, with no deny rule at all. If you picked C, thread 9 is soft; go back to Ch 10 §6 and Ch 12 §3. **D is wrong** — `podSelector` alone covers same-namespace sources; `namespaceSelector` is for crossing namespaces.\n\n*Chapters: 10 (NetworkPolicy semantics, absent-component pattern), 9 (CNI as the pluggable interface).*","numLines":5,"startLine":819,"totalLines":940}}}
